! Resting cavity under a SLOPING ice shelf — the QUASI-GEOPOTENTIAL leg.
!
! *** THIS CASE IS THE MEASUREMENT, AND THE MEASUREMENT IS BAD. ***  It is
! DELIBERATELY NOT in `tests/regression/stability_manifest.py`: it is a
! diagnostic for the vanished-layer corrections (P6.6-P6.8), not a gate,
! and a case whose outcome is toolchain-dependent (NaN on one, saturation
! on the other) cannot be carried as a scoped XFAIL.  Add it to the suite when those
! corrections land, not before, and do NOT make it pass by shortening it,
! by widening a bar or by adding viscosity.  The P6.2 gate that DOES pass
! is its flat-lid sibling, `cavity_flat_lid_rest_zfixed.nml` (bit-zero).
!
! MEASURED (gfortran 15.1, Release, single rank, pred_corr, 30 days
! requested):
!
!                             sigma leg        z_fixed (this file)
!   accel. at step 1 (rms)    1.40E-09 m/s2    6.62E-08 m/s2   (47x worse)
!   En, day  1                1.0-2.1E-09      2.783E-06       (~3 decades)
!   En, day 30                3.043E-08        3.845E-04  (nvfortran GPU)
!   outcome                   completes        NaN during day 18 (gfortran)
!                                              completes         (nvfortran GPU)
!
!   The two toolchains agree on the PHYSICS (day-1 En 2.783E-06 gfortran
!   vs 2.818E-06 nvfortran/GPU, 1.3 % apart) and diverge only on how an
!   unstable run ends: gfortran reaches a non-finite state on day 18,
!   nvfortran saturates instead and finishes at 3.845E-04 -- four
!   decades above the sigma leg, i.e. 1.4 cm/s of spurious current in a
!   cavity that is supposed to be at rest.  Neither outcome is usable
!   and neither is a toolchain bug; the case is simply past the point
!   where its answer means anything.
!
!   (En day 1 for this file, measured before the filler tracer hold
!   landed, was 2.783E-06 m2/s2, ~4 decades above the sigma leg's own
!   day-1 plateau of 1.0-2.1E-09.)
!
! WHY.  The interior tilt IS gone — the flat-lid sibling is bit-zero, so
! the geopotential interfaces truncate nothing where the draft is
! uniform.  What replaces it is the ice-base STAIRCASE: where the draft
! crosses a nominal level the two columns' filler counts differ by one,
! the interface offset across that face jumps by up to `h_nominal`, and
! the FV-MOM6 Pass-2/Pass-3 acceleration in a vanished layer is
! `h`-INDEPENDENT (numerator O(delta-e), denominator -> 0).  Note this is
! NOT the filler-DENSITY mechanism the phase design derives (2.0E-8 m/s2
! from `rho' = -27.6 kg/m3`): on this branch `eos_linear_impl` already
! substitutes `(T_ref, S_ref)` for `h <= H_VANISHED`, so with
! `rho_ref = rho_0 = 1027.51` a filler's density anomaly is EXACTLY zero
! and that term cannot be the source.  It is the geometry term, which
! needs Yung et al. (2026) §3.3.1 (vanished-layer viscosity upwinding),
! §3.3.2 (top-side MWIPG) and §3.2 (interior reference interface) — in
! that order, and none of them is in this build.
!
! This is the z_fixed twin of `cavity_sloping_lid_rest.nml`.  Read that
! file first: the geometry, the stratification, the load partition, the
! zero-viscosity / zero-drag / zero-mixing envelope and the reason the
! initial condition uses `&ocean_zinit_nml source = "linear"` are all
! identical and are documented there.  What follows is ONLY the delta and
! what the delta is expected to do.
!
! THE DELTA — two lines.
!
!   1. `&vcoord_nml vcoord_type = "z_fixed"` (was "sigma").
!   2. `&ocean_cavity_dyn_nml h_min_cavity = 96.0` (was 40.0), forced by
!      the configure-time rule `h_min_cavity >= 2*h_nominal` with
!      `h_nominal = max_depth/nz_layers = 720/15 = 48 m`.  This is
!      ISOMIP+'s own minimum-column rule (Asay-Davis et al. 2016, GMD 9,
!      2471, §3.1.5: "approximately two grid cells").  It is NOT a
!      confound here: the thinnest water column in this domain is 226 m,
!      so 0 of 288 columns are grounded at EITHER value and the grounding
!      line does not move between the two legs.  Everything else —
!      48 x 6 x 15, dx = 2 km, dt = 600 s, 30 days, the draft, the EOS,
!      the IC — is byte-identical to the sigma leg.
!
! WHAT THE COORDINATE DOES.  Under sigma the 15 interfaces TILT with the
! ice base on every column, and it is that tilt the FV-MOM6 pressure
! gradient has to integrate across.  Under z_fixed the interfaces are
! GEOPOTENTIAL: they sit at fixed depths `(nz - k)*48 m` below z = 0
! whatever the draft is, the layers that outcrop into the ice vanish to
! the inert filler `zstar_h_min` and stack under the ice base, and the
! first live layer is CUT by the draft into a partial top cell (Yung,
! Hallberg, Adcroft & Morrison 2026, JAMES 18, e2025MS005645, Fig. 1b;
! Losch 2008, JGR 113 C08043 §2.1 for the partial top cell).  So the
! interior tilt — and with it the sigma truncation the sigma leg
! measures — is STRUCTURALLY absent, and what is left is confined to the
! staircase at the ice base where the filler count changes column to
! column.
!
! WHAT WAS EXPECTED, AND WHY IT WAS THE WRONG EXPECTATION.  The phase
! design predicts a residual from the fillers' DENSITY: a top filler
! carries `hTr = 0` (the ALE remap's drain gate zeroes a vanished cell's
! content), so a column builder that forms `T = hTr/H_FLOOR` reads
! `T = S = 0` and, under the ISOMIP+ linear EOS, `rho' ~ -27.6 kg/m3`.
! That is a real hazard for the RECONSTRUCT column builder
! (`&ocean_pgf_nml reconstruct_for_pressure`), which is where the design
! derived it.  It is NOT what this file runs: on the default
! `rho_layer` path `eos_linear_impl` already substitutes `(T_ref, S_ref)`
! for `h <= H_VANISHED`, so a filler's density is exactly `rho_0` and,
! with `rho_ref = rho_0`, its anomaly is exactly zero.  The measured
! residual is therefore the GEOMETRY term, not the density term, and
! substituting live T/S at consumption would not remove it.
!
! THE V1 ENVELOPE.  `z_fixed` x cavity is ADIABATIC DYNAMICS ONLY until
! the shared `k_top(i,j)` lands (the first live layer, counting down):
! until then `k = nz` is an inert filler on every ice-covered column and
! every consumer that indexes it literally is wrong there.
! `validate_config` refuses basal melt, ice-shelf top drag, KPP, EPBL,
! the ideal-age tracer, GM / Redi / isopycnal slopes, a non-zero
! `kappa_h` and a non-zero `regrid_time_scale` under this combination,
! each naming its follow-up.  Atmospheric forcing is NOT refused: the
! cover mask already zeroes wind stress, surface heat/salt, shortwave and
! restoring on every covered column, and an open-ocean column has
! `z_top = 0` so its `k = nz` is live.  This file is at rest with none of
! it anyway.
!
! `split_scheme` is DELIBERATELY not pinned, exactly as in the sigma leg.

&sim_nml
   sim_type = "ocean"
/

&grid_nml
   nx     = 48
   ny     = 6
   dx     = 2000.0
   dy     = 2000.0
   nghost = 2
/

&time_nml
   t_end        = 2592000.0   ! 30 days
   dt_fixed     = 600.0       ! 10 min outer
   cfl_interval = 1
/

&physics_nml
   coriolis_f    = -1.409e-4   ! f-plane at 75 S (ISOMIP+ 3.1.1)
   wind_stress_x = 0.0
   wind_stress_y = 0.0
/

&nonhydrostatic_nml
   nz_layers = 15
/

&vcoord_nml
   vcoord_type = "z_fixed"     ! quasi-geopotential: does NOT follow the ice
                               ! base.  h_nominal = max_depth/nz = 48 m.
/

&ocean_topo_nml
   topo_config    = "flat"
   max_depth      = 720.0      ! ISOMIP+ z_b,deep; also sets z_fixed_h_ref
   wind_config    = "constant"
   taux_magnitude = 0.0
   coriolis_beta  = 0.0
   coriolis_y_ref = 0.0
/

&ocean_cavity_dyn_nml
   enable       = .true.
   draft_config = "linear"
   draft_depth  = 570.0        ! draft AT draft_x0
   draft_slope  = -6.9e-3      ! shallows toward the calving front
   draft_x0     = -10000.0     ! anchor OUTSIDE the domain so ghosts are iced
   draft_x1     = 72000.0      ! the CALVING FRONT; open ocean beyond
   h_min_cavity = 96.0         ! = 2*h_nominal, ISOMIP+ 3.1.5.  Nothing is
                               ! grounded at 40 or at 96 (min column 226 m).
/

&ocean_pgf_nml
   form          = "fv_mom6"   ! the only form with an injectable top BC
   p_top_in_bc   = .true.      ! REQUIRED for a varying draft
   maxvel        = 2.0
/

&ocean_eos_nml
   eos = "linear"
/

&ocean_ic_nml
   alpha_T = 3.8356948e-2      ! rho_0 * 3.733e-5 /degC   (ISOMIP+)
   beta_S  = 8.0587609e-1      ! rho_0 * 7.843e-4 /PSU    (ISOMIP+)
   T_ref   = -1.0              ! ISOMIP+ Table 4
   S_ref   = 34.2
   rho_0   = 1027.51
/

&ocean_zinit_nml
   enable    = .true.
   source    = "linear"        ! analytic T(z)/S(z) at the TRUE geopotential
                               ! depth.  Under z_fixed the layer centres are
                               ! seeded FROM the target grid, so the profile
                               ! is exact on the running coordinate and the
                               ! first remap is an identity.
   lin_t_ref = -1.9            ! ISOMIP+ COLD: T0 = T_bot, no thermal gradient
   lin_dt_dz = 0.0
   lin_s_ref = 33.8            ! S at z = 0
   lin_ds_dz = -1.0416667e-3   ! (33.8 - 34.55)/720, z positive UP
/

&tracer_nml
   ! Overwritten by the zinit overlay on the interior AND the ghosts; kept
   ! consistent so a reader is not misled about the state being seeded.
   initial_temperature = -1.9
   initial_salinity    = 34.175
/

&ocean_coriolis_nml
   form = "sadourny"
/

&ocean_hvisc_nml
   ! Zero, deliberately — see the sigma leg.  It matters more here, not
   ! less: a z-like coordinate's remaining error lives at the ice-base
   ! staircase, and viscosity is exactly what would hide it.
   nu_h = 0.0
   nu_4 = 0.0
/

&ocean_bdrag_nml
   ! No drag: the measurement must not be flattered by dissipation.
   form = "quadratic"
   cd   = 0.0
/

&ocean_vmix_nml
   use_closure = .false.       ! pure dyn-core: no mixing anywhere
   use_kpp     = .false.       ! also REQUIRED under z_fixed x cavity (v1)
/

&ocean_bt_nml
   ! split_scheme is DELIBERATELY not pinned: the default (pred_corr) is the
   ! base case and the stability suite builds the __ssp_rk2 twin from the
   ! same file.  Pinning either would delete that comparison.
   auto_n_inner = .true.
/

&ocean_diag_nml
   enabled  = .true.
   filename = "cavity_sloping_lid_rest_zfixed"
   dt_out   = 86400.0          ! daily
/

&output_nml
   output_dir     = "./out_cavity_sloping_lid_rest_zfixed"
   output_to_file = .false.
/

&logging_nml
   log_level       = "info"
   status_interval = 86400.0
/
